#
# Each line is a `<name> <value>` pair in the same format the diagnostic
# protocol's `conf set` takes, so this file also works with:
#
#     moteus_tool -t @MOTEUS_CONTROLLER_ID@ --write-config current_config.cfg
#
# Every key here was verified to exist on the attached board with
# `moteus_tool --dump-config`.  This board exposes aux2 only -- it has no
# aux1.* configuration keys at all -- so nothing below references aux1.
#
# EVERY peripheral on the port is set explicitly, including the ones being
# left disabled.  This is deliberate: a peripheral left at a stale value can
# claim pins that another one needs, which makes the port fail validation.
# That is exactly what `aux2.uart.mode 5` did -- it held the UART pins while
# SPI wanted them, so aux2 reported `error.uart_pin_error` and spi.active
# stayed False.  Setting each mode explicitly keeps that from recurring.
#
# Pin modes:  0 NC   1 SPI   2 SPI_CS   3 UART   4 SW_QUAD   5 HW_QUAD
#             6 HALL   7 INDEX   8 SINE   9 COSINE   13 I2C   14 DIN
#             15 DOUT   16 AIN   17 PWM_OUT
# Pin pulls:  0 none   1 pull-up   2 pull-down
# SPI modes:  0 onboard AS5047P   1 disabled   2 AS5047P   3 iC-PZ
#             4 MA732   5 MA600   8 AMT22   9 RLS Orbis
# UART modes: 0 disabled   1 RLS AksIM-2   2 tunnel   3 debug
#             4 CUI AMT21x RS422   5 fdcanusb serial

# --- Pins -------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins 0-2 are CLK/MISO/MOSI, pin 3 is chip select for the MA600.
aux2.pins.0.mode @AUX2_PIN0_MODE@
